@page "/Levels"
@model Alpha6Ops.Server.Pages.LevelsModel
@inject ServerSettings Settings
@{ ViewData["Title"] = "Levels"; }
<div class="page-heading pricing-heading">
    <h1>Fly free. Grow when your operation does.</h1>
    <p class="lead">One account covers your own flying and every airline you belong to. Personal and airline levels are separate, so a pilot on the free level can still fly for a Pro airline.</p>
    <p class="early-access" role="status">Early access: every level is complimentary. Choose one from your account and it applies immediately. Paid levels and their prices will be announced before public release — nothing is charged until then.</p>
</div>

<div class="strip-board" aria-label="Levels">
    <div class="strip-group">Personal</div>
    @foreach (var tier in Alpha6Ops.Server.Pages.LevelsModel.Tiers.Where(t => t.Group == "Personal")) { <partial name="_TierStrip" model="tier" /> }
    <div class="strip-group">Airline</div>
    @foreach (var tier in Alpha6Ops.Server.Pages.LevelsModel.Tiers.Where(t => t.Group == "Airline")) { <partial name="_TierStrip" model="tier" /> }
</div>

<section class="grid two pay-grid" aria-label="Paying and starting">
    <article class="card pay-card">
        <h2>How you'll pay, when the time comes</h2>
        <p>Paid levels will check out with <strong>Link</strong>, the one-tap wallet from Stripe: your email, a one-time code, and a saved card you never re-type. Anyone without Link sees a normal card form on the same page. Alpha 6 never sees or stores card numbers.</p>
        <div class="link-mock" aria-hidden="true"><span class="link-pill">Pay with Link</span><span class="link-or">or card · Apple Pay · Google Pay</span></div>
        <ul class="plain">
            <li>Cancel any time from your account; the level runs to the end of the period you paid for.</li>
            <li>Airline levels are paid by the airline's owner and cover every crew member.</li>
            <li>Receipts and card changes live in a billing page linked from your account.</li>
        </ul>
    </article>
    <article class="card pay-card">
        <h2>Start in three steps</h2>
        <ol class="steps-list">
            <li><strong>Create your account.</strong> Email and password, a passkey, or your Microsoft or Google sign-in. Verify your email from the message we send.</li>
            <li><strong>Download Alpha 6 OPS for Windows.</strong> Sign in once; the app remembers you and works offline for your next flights.</li>
            <li><strong>Fly.</strong> Log flights on your own, join a crew with an invitation code, or found your own airline.</li>
        </ol>
        <div class="actions">
            @if (Model.SignedIn) { <a class="button" href="/Account/Plan">Choose your level</a> }
            else if (Settings.IsConfigured) { <a class="button" href="/auth/signup">Create an account</a><a class="button secondary" href="/auth/login">Sign in</a> }
            else { <a class="button" href="/Download">Download</a> }
            <a href="/Download">Download for Windows</a>
        </div>
    </article>
</section>

<section class="faq" aria-label="Questions">
    <h2>Questions people ask first</h2>
    <dl class="faq-list">
        <dt>Do I need a paid level to fly for an airline?</dt><dd>No. Airline membership is free at every personal level. Only the owner's choice of airline level affects the airline.</dd>
        <dt>What happens to my logbook if I stop paying?</dt><dd>Nothing is deleted. Your flights stay in your logbook; the level returns to Flying as a Pilot and premium features pause.</dd>
        <dt>Can one account own more than one airline?</dt><dd>One Community airline per owner. Pro airlines don't count toward that limit.</dd>
        <dt>Which simulator does this support?</dt><dd>Microsoft Flight Simulator 2024 on Windows. Live SimConnect tracking is in testing; replay works today.</dd>
    </dl>
</section>
